before leaving on a road trip Tiffani  filled up her gas tank which holds 16  gallons of gas after four hours tiffany  noticed that the gas tank was 7/8 full  let me do that in a different color was  7/8 full how many gallons of gas were  left in the tank and actually doesn't in  any way matter on how many how long she  had to drive so you this is actually  just extra information that you can  ignore for the sake of this problem so  7/8 full another way of reading that is  7/8 if we wanted to put units here  that's 7/8 is number of gallons left  number of gallons left per total number  of gallons per total number of gallons  so this is saying if you take number of  gallons left divided by total number of  gallons it's essentially 7/8 it doesn't  mean that there are 7 gallons left and  there were 8 total gallons it just means  that the ratio between the number of  gallons left and the total is 7/8 and if  we multiply that times 16 total gallons  times 16 total total gallons you see  that the total gallons cancel out with  the total gallons and the only units  your left is number of gallons left and  you're essentially just multiplying 7  eighths multiplying 7 eighths times 16  so this becomes 7 over 8 times 16 and  you could even view that as 16 over 1  and this is the number of gallons left  so these are the only units we have left  number of gallons and so we can multiply  it out or we can simplify it ahead of  time we could say this is 7 times 16  over 8 times 1 but both the numerator  and the denominator is divisible by 8 so  let's divide this by 8 so let's divide  by 8 and let's divide by 8 this 8 and  this 8 will cancel out 16 divided by 8  is 2 so we get 7 times 2 is 14 over 1  which is the same thing as 14 gallons  left so we're done how many gallons were  left in the tank  14 is essentially just 7 eighths the  fraction that's full times the total  number of gallons that the tank can hold
 

